/       QUESTIONS:
/1.  SEA SERPENT STORIES USUALLY ORIGINATE
/(A) AMONG SUPERSTITIOUS PEOPLE
/(B) THROUGH PUBLICITY ATTEMPTS
/(C) AS JOKES
/(D) IN SIGHTING OF SERPENTLIKE CREATURES
	D
/2.  THE MOST RECENT SEA SERPENT REPORTED IN THIS
/    ARTICLE WAS SEEN IN
/(A) 1954
/(B) 1955
/(C) 1855
/(D) 1808
	B
/3.  WHAT MESSAGE FOR NEWSPAPER READERS IS CONTAINED IN
/    THIS SELECTION?
/(A) AN EDITORIAL CRITICIZING EXAGGERATED REPORTS OF
/    SEA SERPENTS
/(B) THE FALSE REPORT OF A SEA MONSTER BY A VACATIONING
/    EDITOR
/(C) A COLLECTION OF DIFFERENT LEGENDS OF SEA SNAKES
/(D) A DESCRIPTION OF REAL SEA SERPENTS
	B
/4.  REPTILES CANNOT LIVE IN DEEP WATER BECAUSE
/(A) THEY ARE UNABLE TO SWIM WELL
/(B) THEY BREATHE USING LUNGS
/(C) THEY CAN NEVER WITHSTAND GREAT WATER PRESSURE
/(D) THEY CANNOT REPRODUCE THERE
	B
/5.  SEA SNAKES ARE FOUND IN
/(A) THE ATLANTIC OCEAN
/(B) THE SCOTTISH LAKES
/(C) THE PANAMA CANAL
/(D) THE INDIAN OCEAN
	D
/6.  MOST OF THE SEA SERPENTS REPORTED ARE
/(A) WHALES
/(B) OARFISH
/(C) SHARKS
/(D) WATER SNAKES
	B
/7.  THE SECRETARY OF THE SMITHSONIAN INSTITUTION WAS
/(A) SPENCER BAIRD
/(B) COVINGTON SMITH
/(C) KEITH MCRAE
/(D) JOHN FITCH
	A
/8.  SEA SNAKES BELONG TO THE FAMILY OF
/(A) BOIDAE
/(B) VIPERIDAE
/(C) HYDROPHIIDAE
/(D) VIVERRIDAE
	C
/9.  THE FICTITIOUS SEA SERPENT FOUND IN NEW YORK WAS
/    ALLEGEDLY KILLED BY
/(A) A HARPOON
/(B) A RIFLE
/(C) A KNIFE
/(D) A DEADLY FISHING HOOK
	A
/10. THE FOLLOWING IS NOT A TRUE STATEMENT ABOUT SEA
/    SNAKES
/(A) THEY ARE HARMLESS
/(B) THEY ARE FAIRLY SMALL
/(C) THEY DO NOT COME ASHORE
/(D) THEY GROUP TOGETHER
	A
